1
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:03,434
It looks like a gift.

2
00:00:04,134 --> 00:00:07,948
OpenAI says more than 1 billion people use it every week.

3
00:00:07,948 --> 00:00:09,955
The vast majority pay nothing.

4
00:00:10,655 --> 00:00:12,101
So what are you paying with?

5
00:00:17,701 --> 00:00:19,572
November 30, 2022.

6
00:00:19,572 --> 00:00:21,963
ChatGPT launches, free.

7
00:00:22,343 --> 00:00:24,377
Critics called it unreliable.

8
00:00:24,377 --> 00:00:26,552
A million users came in 5 days.

9
00:00:26,932 --> 00:00:27,518
Why free?

10
00:00:27,518 --> 00:00:30,904
OpenAI's launch post says: "to get users' feedback."

11
00:00:31,354 --> 00:00:34,967
And the next model, GPT-4, had already finished training.

12
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:37,185
Three months before you said hello.

13
00:00:37,785 --> 00:00:42,259
Scale built it: bigger models, more data, more compute, predictably better.

14
00:00:42,639 --> 00:00:47,969
Then OpenAI refined it, partly with "feedback submitted by ChatGPT users."

15
00:00:48,469 --> 00:00:50,700
The free product was shaping the next one.

16
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,156
It has a name: the data flywheel.

17
00:00:54,536 --> 00:00:55,176
You use it.

18
00:00:55,176 --> 00:00:56,863
Your feedback becomes signal.

19
00:00:56,863 --> 00:00:57,969
The model improves.

20
00:00:57,969 --> 00:00:58,958
More people come.

21
00:00:59,458 --> 00:01:05,150
OpenAI said "thumbs-up and thumbs-down data from ChatGPT" became a reward signal.

22
00:01:05,530 --> 00:01:09,971
It helped make the model so flattering that OpenAI rolled the update back.

23
00:01:09,971 --> 00:01:11,231
Your clicks steer it.

24
00:01:11,781 --> 00:01:13,153
You're not just the customer.

25
00:01:13,153 --> 00:01:14,336
You're part of the wheel.

26
00:01:15,836 --> 00:01:17,877
Startups rush to wrap the models.

27
00:01:18,257 --> 00:01:20,818
Then ChatGPT learned to read PDFs.

28
00:01:20,818 --> 00:01:24,283
One reaction: "Many startups just died today."

29
00:01:24,783 --> 00:01:27,797
Sam Altman's warning: bet that the models won't improve,

30
00:01:27,797 --> 00:01:29,358
and you'll get "steamrolled."

31
00:01:29,858 --> 00:01:31,353
Each model opens doors.

32
00:01:31,353 --> 00:01:33,432
The next release can close them.

33
00:01:34,932 --> 00:01:36,606
The wheel reaches the coders.

34
00:01:36,986 --> 00:01:39,862
Big employers made it official: use AI.

35
00:01:40,242 --> 00:01:45,538
In 2023, AI could solve 2% of real GitHub issues on a benchmark.

36
00:01:45,918 --> 00:01:52,229
By February 2026, Anthropic reported about 80% for Claude Opus 4.6.

37
00:01:52,609 --> 00:01:58,201
Then Claude Opus 5.5, which Anthropic puts at the level of its bigger Fable model

38
00:01:58,201 --> 00:01:59,099
on most work.

39
00:01:59,599 --> 00:02:03,010
On personal plans, your code can feed the wheel too.

40
00:02:03,010 --> 00:02:06,552
In GitHub's words: "Real-world data = smarter models."

41
00:02:08,052 --> 00:02:09,743
So why is it nearly free?

42
00:02:10,243 --> 00:02:11,480
Investor billions.

43
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,649
A race for users.

44
00:02:12,649 --> 00:02:12,924
Ads.

45
00:02:12,924 --> 00:02:13,886
Falling costs.

46
00:02:14,386 --> 00:02:16,873
And part of the price is paid in data.

47
00:02:16,873 --> 00:02:17,266
Yours.

48
00:02:18,016 --> 00:02:19,263
You can switch it off.

49
00:02:19,263 --> 00:02:21,473
Most people never touch their defaults.

50
00:02:21,853 --> 00:02:23,704
It's a trade, and often a good one.

51
00:02:24,084 --> 00:02:28,418
But if your plan is a thin wrapper around someone else's model, please, wait.

52
00:02:28,418 --> 00:02:29,319
The wheel won't.

53
00:02:31,219 --> 00:02:32,167
Still, go ahead.

54
00:02:32,167 --> 00:02:32,523
Build.

55
00:02:32,523 --> 00:02:33,234
Raise money.

56
00:02:33,234 --> 00:02:33,530
Ship.

57
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:36,433
But your biggest asset is not on that list.

58
00:02:37,033 --> 00:02:38,029
Your attention.

59
00:02:38,029 --> 00:02:42,015
We now stay on one screen about 47 seconds before switching.

60
00:02:42,015 --> 00:02:42,613
Guard it.

61
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:43,799
Your mind.

62
00:02:43,799 --> 00:02:48,884
In Anthropic's own trial, coders learning with AI scored 17 points lower on what

63
00:02:48,884 --> 00:02:50,155
they'd just learned.

64
00:02:50,155 --> 00:02:50,727
Train it.

65
00:02:51,277 --> 00:02:53,643
Your body, and your mental health.

66
00:02:53,643 --> 00:02:57,818
People who exercise report 43% fewer bad mental-health days.

67
00:02:57,818 --> 00:02:58,375
Move it.

68
00:02:58,975 --> 00:03:00,715
No release will update you.

69
00:03:00,715 --> 00:03:01,553
Only you can.

70
00:03:02,353 --> 00:03:03,637
Invest consciously.

